Braised Asparagus
Serves: 4
Prep: 5 min
Cook: 10 min
Total: 15 min
Source: Serious Eats, J. Kenji López-Alt
Equipment: 30 cm straight-sided sauté pan with lid

Braise (heat, 7–10 min): Add stock and butter and **cover at once**. Cook until tender and glazed. If it dries out first, add **a few Tbsp water**. Serve at once.
  Sear (heat, 3 min): Oil **lightly smoking** over high heat. Asparagus in one layer, season. **1½ min** untouched, shake, **1½ min** more. One pan per **450 g**.
    - 2 Tbsp | Vegetable oil
    Trim: Cut off the woody ends. Peel the lower stalks if you like.
      - 450 g = 1 lb | Green asparagus
    - to taste | Kosher salt & pepper
  - 240 ml = 1 cup | Chicken stock | low-sodium, or vegetable
  - 40 g = 3 Tbsp | Unsalted butter
